{
  "id": 440187964,
  "iid": 22737,
  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "epan: Use unsigned offsets with tvb_*_length_remaining",
  "description": "There has never been much reason to use negative offsets with\ntvb_captured_length_remaining, and there do not appear to be any\nsuch uses in the repository. It's possible to perhaps construct\na reason with tvb_reported_length_remaining, but only if the user\nknows that negative offsets refer to the captured length, and it's\nstill not the simplest way to do it. There don't appear to be any\nsuch uses either.\n\nIt is much more likely that a negative offset passed in is the\nresult of overflow (positive overflow, or negative after subtraction)\nand treating as a value from the end of the captured length can lead\nat worst to infinite loops.\n\nPing #20103",
  "state": "merged",
